# Privacy Policy — AVIANTO TECH

**Last updated:** 12 October 2026

## 1. Introduction

AVIANTO TECH is developing ALIGN (AI-enabled Learning–Industry Graduate Nexus), a research project focused on analysing computing education and industry skill requirements.

This policy explains how information is handled by the ALIGN research application.

## 2. Information Processed

Depending on the features implemented, ALIGN may process:

- Job titles, company names, locations, posting dates, descriptions and source URLs from publicly available or authorised sources.
- Skills and technologies identified from job descriptions.
- Academic, technology and industry evidence authorised for research.
- Technical information required to operate and secure the application.

ALIGN is not intended to collect LinkedIn passwords or authentication credentials.

## 3. Purpose of Processing

Information may be used to analyse industry skill requirements, compare them with computing curricula, identify potential skill gaps, study emerging technologies and generate research findings.

## 4. Data Collection

Data collection must comply with applicable laws, source-specific terms and access permissions. Public availability does not automatically permit automated collection.

## 5. Security and Retention

Reasonable safeguards will be used to protect stored information. Access to non-public research data should be limited to authorised users, and data should be retained only as long as necessary for the stated purposes.

## 6. Sharing

Information may be shared with authorised project collaborators or academic supervisors when necessary for the research. Personal or confidential information should not be disclosed without an appropriate legal basis or permission.

## 7. Third-Party Services

The application may use third-party platforms for hosting, development or data processing. Those services may have their own privacy policies and terms.

## 8. Policy Updates

This policy may be updated as the application develops. The latest version will be published on this page.

